"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"not_legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{U}","name":"Winged Sliver","oracle_id":"24e96682-14ca-4a62-a920-2d686c8a5dbf","oracle_text":"All Sliver creatures have flying.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Sliver"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":["Equip"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}","name":"Wolfhunter's Quiver","oracle_id":"f1ebccc2-d12a-4440-8a73-86c1bc901feb","oracle_text":"Equipped creature has \"{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target\" and \"{T}: This creature deals 3 damage to target Werewolf creature.\"\nEquip {5}","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2012-02-03","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact \u2014 Equipment"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{0}","name":"Generic Composite Werewolf","oracle_id":"fixture:composite-werewolf","oracle_text":"","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2011-05-14","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature \u2014 Werewolf"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A land that's a Forest has the intrinsic mana ability \"{T}: Add {G}.\"","oracle_id":"162572f2-1757-42e9-bd97-e6bd9a762c0e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"As long as Ashaya is on the battlefield, it's affected by its second ability and thus its first ability counts itself.","oracle_id":"162572f2-1757-42e9-bd97-e6bd9a762c0e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to Ashaya may become lethal if lands you control leave the battlefield during that turn.","oracle_id":"162572f2-1757-42e9-bd97-e6bd9a762c0e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability that defines Ashaya's power and toughness applies in all zones, not just the battlefield.","oracle_id":"162572f2-1757-42e9-bd97-e6bd9a762c0e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't play creature cards as lands; you'll still have to cast them as spells, and they'll enter the battlefield as lands (in addition to their other types).","oracle_id":"162572f2-1757-42e9-bd97-e6bd9a762c0e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like flying, having more than one instance of the ability doesn\u2019t provide any additional benefit.","oracle_id":"24e96682-14ca-4a62-a920-2d686c8a5dbf","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the creature type of a Sliver changes so it\u2019s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures.","oracle_id":"24e96682-14ca-4a62-a920-2d686c8a5dbf","published_at":"2013-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has the supertype world. When a world permanent enters, any world permanents that were already on the battlefield are put into their owners' graveyards. This is a state-based action called the \"world rule.\" The new world permanent stays on the battlefield. If two world permanents enter at the same time, they're both put into their owners' graveyards.","oracle_id":"30e99293-3212-4e3f-b543-b1c7c416575d","published_at":"2008-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature is subject to the \"summoning sickness\" rule: It can only attack, and its {T} abilities can only be activated, if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn.","oracle_id":"30e99293-3212-4e3f-b543-b1c7c416575d","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The decision whether or not to tap or untap is made on resolution. This is not a modal spell.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not a toggle effect. If you use Twiddle to tap a card and before it takes effect your opponent taps it, Twiddle will not automatically untap the card.","oracle_id":"773ad2ef-5acc-49ea-8d85-056330e87039","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the target land is an illegal target by the time Lithoform Blight tries to resolve, the spell doesn't resolve. It doesn't enter the battlefield, so you don't draw a card.","oracle_id":"b256c311-e37d-4b3c-889c-85443e3d5e7e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The enchanted land keeps any other card types (such as artifact) and supertypes (such as basic or legendary) when it loses its land types.","oracle_id":"b256c311-e37d-4b3c-889c-85443e3d5e7e","published_at":"2020-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect causes Dress Down to become a creature, it will lose its own abilities along with all other creatures. This includes the triggered ability that causes it to be sacrificed at the beginning of the end step.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect grants a creature an ability after Dress Down has entered the battlefield, it won't lose that ability. For example, if a land becomes a creature while Dress Down is on the battlefield, it will still gain any abilities given to it by the effect that animated it. It will, however, lose any abilities it already had.","oracle_id":"c1cbbda0-e02b-4b9c-8669-ea87ca629520","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"For each of the activated abilities, the equipped creature is the source of the ability and the damage. For example, if the equipped creature is not an artifact, you could activate either ability targeting a creature with protection from artifacts.","oracle_id":"f1ebccc2-d12a-4440-8a73-86c1bc901feb","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Only the equipped creature\u2019s controller can activate the abilities it gains from Wolfhunter\u2019s Quiver.","oracle_id":"f1ebccc2-d12a-4440-8a73-86c1bc901feb","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You could activate the first ability targeting a Werewolf creature if you wanted to.","oracle_id":"f1ebccc2-d12a-4440-8a73-86c1bc901feb","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a permanent has an ability that causes itself to be a land, such as that of Ashaya, Soul of the Wild, that ability will apply to it even though it loses that ability due to Toxicrene. This is because type-changing effects are always applied before any effects that add or remove abilities. It will still have \"{T}: Add one mana of any color\" and lose all other abilities.","oracle_id":"fbfe98f0-110b-4d4b-9240-2767b08acf68","published_at":"2022-10-07","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
